# A ledger changes through a method of its own: `ledger.add(..)` takes the ledger as it was and makes it at its own
# moment, and inside it `this.rows.push(e)` runs on the ledger's rows and makes the ledger anew. `refiled` copies the
# expense it is handed and hands back the copy; `merged` builds a new Ledger from the rows of both; `remove` sends a
# delete through the client the route is handed, and `main` drops what it gives. `counted` copies the Map (a library
# operation whose result it names) and sets a key of the copy. The route's parameter `api` is a value from its start;
# an object literal no step makes is a value from beyond.
route ledger.ledger.main
step main/Ledger()
step main/refiled
step main/Ledger.add
step main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push
step main/remove
step main/Ledger()#2
step main/Ledger.merged
step main/Ledger.merged/Ledger()
step main/withLine
step main/counted
step main/counted/set

line entry > main call
line Api·api > main value
line main/Ledger() > Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() value
line Expense > main/refiled value
line main/refiled > Expense@main/refiled value
line Expense@main/refiled > main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push value
line main/Ledger.add > Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.add value
line main/Ledger()#2 > Ledger@main/Ledger()#2 value
line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.add > main/Ledger.merged value              # merged reads this.rows itself
line Ledger@main/Ledger()#2 > main/Ledger.merged value                     # and other.rows
line main/Ledger.merged/Ledger() > Ledger·out@main/Ledger.merged/Ledger() value
line Ledger·out@main/Ledger.merged/Ledger() > main/Ledger.merged value
line main/Ledger.merged > Ledger@main/Ledger.merged value
line Ledger@main/Ledger.merged > main value                                # main counts its rows
line main/withLine > main back
line main/counted/set > _·out@main/counted/set value
line main/counted > main back

home Api·api main
home Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() main
home Expense main
home Expense@main/refiled main
home Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.add main
home Ledger@main/Ledger()#2 main
home Ledger·out@main/Ledger.merged/Ledger() main/Ledger.merged
home Ledger@main/Ledger.merged main
home _·out@main/counted/set main/counted

side entry left

# An operation that changes a part of the receiver (`this.rows.push(e)`) takes what it is handed but neither runs on
# nor makes anew the receiver, which ends at the method's own arrow
known #129 line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() > main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push value
known #129 line main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push > Ledger·this@main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push value
known #129 line Ledger·this@main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push > main/Ledger.add value
known #129 home Ledger·this@main/Ledger.add/this.rows.push main/Ledger.add
known #129 extra line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() > main/Ledger.add value

# A call on a field of a network client's type (`api.http.delete(..)`, `http: AxiosInstance`) is a request through
# the client the route is handed; the code names no host, so its place is `Web`. A DELETE leaves something there, and
# main drops what it answers
line main/remove > Web own
side Web right
line Api·api > main/remove value

# A library operation whose result the body names is a step (`const out = new Map(m)`); one whose result it does not
# name is none, and what it gives goes into the call around it (`out.get(k) ?? 0`, whose left always runs: no choice)
step main/counted/Map()
line main/counted/Map() > _·out@main/counted/Map() value
line _·out@main/counted/Map() > main/counted/set value
home _·out@main/counted/Map() main/counted

# A result the caller drops (`void remove(..)`) goes back to it
known #134 extra line main/remove > main back

# The own arrow takes a value its body only hands to a step inside it: the expense `refiled` gives, handed to `add`
known #126 extra line Expense@main/refiled > main value

# `counted` hands back the Map its `set` made anew
known #101 line _·out@main/counted/set > main/counted value

# a result the caller drops goes back to it: the reader does not say the call is a statement of its own
known #134 extra line main/Ledger.add > main back
